<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 188 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 188 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 188 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.05 BLN   1.05 BLN   1.0 BLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    350 MLN    538 MLN    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BILLS	  =	    14 MLN#    138 MLN#   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BILLS	  =	    12 MLN#     50 MLN#   =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG MARCH 4,5  =	    324 MLN*   =	    =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p># INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
